# Next.js, React, TypeScript

## App Router

- Use the **App Router** (`src/app/`): `layout.tsx`, `page.tsx`, route segments, `metadata` export where appropriate.
- Prefer **Server Components** by default. Add `'use client'` only when you need browser APIs, event handlers, or client-only hooks.

## React

- Use **function components**. Keep pages and sections readable; extract components when a block grows or repeats.
- Set meaningful **`alt` (and `title` when useful)** on `next/image` and other images.

## TypeScript

- Respect **`strict`** typing; avoid `any` unless there is a documented reason.
- Type props explicitly for new components; align with how sibling files in `src/app/` declare types.

## Styling

- Use **Tailwind** utility classes consistent with nearby markup (spacing, typography, layout).
- Prefer `next/image` for images over raw `<img>` when using static imports or remote URLs configured in Next.

## Icons

- SVG/icon components live under `src/app/components/icons/`; re-export from `index.ts` when adding new icons to match the existing barrel pattern.
